      "message": "test(thread): open the hole ahead of main's thread_mill_rim and coarse_rims threads (#992)\n\n#1005's refresh moved main's #1071 / #1073 thread tests onto a thread\nmill; #992's law then refuses each of them for an undrilled hole (the\nstock box stands solid where the model's hole is). Each thread now has a\nflat end-mill Bore of the same declared holes generated ahead, so the\ntests judge the thread's gouge verdict again, not the entry refusal. The\nlaws are unchanged.\n\nRefs #992\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
